{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. Thompson. I'm Dr. Patel, one of your hospitalists. You're here today for your second maintenance dose of high-dose methotrexate for your CNS lymphoma. How have you been feeling since your last admission?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Morning, Doctor. I’ve actually been doing pretty well. No major issues—no nausea, no weakness, and my vision’s stable. Just a little anxious about the chemo again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. It’s completely normal to feel anxious. This is a planned admission, and we’ll be following the same protocol as last time. You tolerated it well before, so we expect the same this round."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I did get some constipation last time, though. Is that likely to happen again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:20:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can happen, since methotrexate and the bowel changes from hospitalization can slow things down. But we’ve already ordered your usual bowel regimen—senna, docusate, and magnesium citrate—to help prevent that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:21:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s reassuring. And my ears have been feeling blocked again—like last time during chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:22:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, cerumen impaction can worsen during chemotherapy. We’ll prescribe ear drops to soften the wax, and that should help clear it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. One more thing—my headaches. They always seem to come back when I’m in the hospital."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:25:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve noted that. It’s likely related to the methotrexate or hospital stress. We’ll monitor it. If it comes on, we can give you Fioricet, which helped last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:26:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. And my reflux—should I keep taking my omeprazole?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:27:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re actually switching you to ranitidine while you’re here. It’s part of the protocol to reduce stomach irritation during high-dose methotrexate. We’ll switch you back to omeprazole when you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And what about my aspirin? I’ve been taking it daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:30:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re holding the aspirin while you’re on methotrexate to reduce bleeding risk, especially since you’re getting heparin for DVT prevention. We’ll restart it at discharge, given your family history of heart disease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. When will the chemo be given?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:32:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "This afternoon, around 4 PM. We’ll start an IV bicarbonate drip beforehand to keep your urine alkaline, which helps protect your kidneys and clear the methotrexate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the leucovorin? When does that start?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2130-10-13 08:35:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "24 hours after the methotrexate infusion begins. It’s a rescue medication to protect your healthy cells. We’ll continue it until your methotrexate levels drop low enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2130-10-13 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi Mr. Thompson. You just finished your methotrexate infusion. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2130-10-13 12:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay so far. A little tired, but no nausea or pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2130-10-13 12:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. We’ll keep monitoring your labs and urine pH. We’ve started the bicarbonate drip as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2130-10-14 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from this morning look stable. Your liver enzymes are starting to rise a bit—ALT and AST—which is expected with methotrexate. Nothing concerning yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2130-10-14 09:21:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous? Last time I was worried about my liver."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2130-10-14 09:22:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a common, temporary side effect. We monitor it closely, and it usually resolves after the methotrexate clears. We’re not seeing any signs of serious liver injury."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2130-10-14 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I haven’t had a bowel movement yet, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2130-10-14 09:25:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We expected that. We’ll keep you on the bowel regimen. If it doesn’t improve, we can add something stronger, but let’s give it a little more time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2130-10-14 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, I’ve got a headache again. It’s not severe, but it’s there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2130-10-14 14:31:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Let me check. No fever, no neurological changes. I’ll order a dose of Fioricet. This is likely a drug-induced headache, common with methotrexate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2130-10-14 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. Will it go away on its own?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2130-10-14 14:34:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, once the methotrexate clears your system. We’ll manage it with medication in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2130-10-15 06:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your methotrexate level this morning was 26—expected this early. Liver enzymes are up but stable. Your urine pH is staying above 7.5, which is perfect."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2130-10-15 06:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the leucovorin? When did that start?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2130-10-15 06:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It started yesterday at 4 PM, exactly 24 hours after your infusion. We’ll keep giving it until your methotrexate level drops below 0.05."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2130-10-15 06:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And when do you think that’ll happen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2130-10-15 06:20:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Based on the trend, likely by tomorrow. We’ll check levels every 12 hours to be sure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2130-10-15 18:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Your methotrexate level dropped to 1.5 this evening. That’s a good sign. Liver enzymes are peaking but still within expected range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2130-10-15 18:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. My ears feel a little better with the drops."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2130-10-15 18:32:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll keep using them until discharge. Any nausea or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2130-10-15 18:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, but I did have a small bowel movement this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2130-10-15 18:35:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. We’ll keep the regimen going to prevent it from coming back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2130-10-16 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your methotrexate level is now 0.05—perfect. We’ll give one more dose of leucovorin and then stop it. You’re clearing the drug well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2130-10-16 06:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great news. Does that mean I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2130-10-16 06:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely tomorrow. We’ll check one final level in the morning to confirm it’s near zero. Your liver enzymes are starting to come down too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2130-10-16 06:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my aspirin and omeprazole—will I restart those?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2130-10-16 06:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, both will be restarted at discharge. We’re holding aspirin until then due to bleeding risk, and we’ll switch back to omeprazole from ranitidine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2130-10-16 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, I feel much better. Headache’s gone, and I’ve had two bowel movements today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2130-10-16 14:01:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. Your last methotrexate level was 0.02—essentially cleared. We’ll plan for discharge tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2130-10-16 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What’s next for follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2130-10-16 14:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue with maintenance therapy as scheduled. Your oncologist will coordinate your next methotrexate dose in about a month."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2130-10-17 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. Thompson. Your labs are stable, and you’re clinically well. We’re clearing you for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2130-10-17 08:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m glad it went smoothly again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2130-10-17 08:32:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. We’re sending you home with aspirin, omeprazole, docusate, and ondansetron for nausea if needed. Use magnesium citrate if constipation returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2130-10-17 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my next chemo?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2130-10-17 08:35:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Same plan—rituximab in clinic, then your next methotrexate dose in about four weeks. Your oncology team will contact you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2130-10-17 08:36:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. Thanks for taking care of me again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2130-10-17 08:37:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call if you have fever, severe nausea, or any new neurological symptoms. Otherwise, see you next time."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2130-10-13 08:07:00",
    "admission_end": "2130-10-17 11:05:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. Thompson was admitted for his second maintenance cycle of high-dose methotrexate for primary central nervous system lymphoma. He had previously completed induction therapy and the first maintenance dose without complications. During this admission, he received high-dose methotrexate on day one, with leucovorin rescue initiated 24 hours later and continued until methotrexate levels dropped to 0.02, at which point it was discontinued. He developed mild, transient transaminitis and a drug-induced headache, both managed supportively. Constipation and cerumen impaction recurred but resolved with standard treatment. Aspirin and omeprazole were held during hospitalization and restarted at discharge. He was discharged home in stable condition with plans to continue outpatient chemotherapy as scheduled.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Primary central nervous system lymphoma, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Hodgkin's disease, unspecified type, intrathoracic lymph nodes",
      "Personal history of tuberculosis",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Dizziness and giddiness",
      "Impacted cerumen",
